@startuml
title Clerk identity and route permissions
hide footbox
actor Client
participant FastAPI as API
participant "app.auth" as Auth
database PostgreSQL as PG
Client -> API: Request (optional Authorization bearer JWT)
API -> Auth: Verify any supplied Clerk session
alt Token supplied
  Auth -> Auth: Require public key / issuer / authorized parties config
  Auth -> Auth: Verify RS256 signature, issuer, exp/nbf/iat, sub/sid, azp
  note over Auth: Invalid session -> 401; missing/invalid config -> 503
  Auth -> PG: Resolve user by verified Clerk subject
  PG --> Auth: Local profile or none
else No token
  Auth -> Auth: Anonymous caller
end
alt POST /users
  Auth --> API: Require verified subject; provision self (no email-based linking)
else Profile / pod collection / pod detail
  Auth --> API: Require local profile; self-only or owned/member pods
else Game list / game detail / result / statistics
  Auth -> PG: Filter/check private pod membership or ownership
  alt Private permission absent
    Auth -> PG: Require owner-approved public pod
    Auth -> PG: For game history: require completed result
  end
  Auth --> API: Authorized read or hidden record (404)
else Mutations
  Auth -> PG: Lock pod; require owner or registered admin
  note over Auth, PG
Visibility, admin grants and pod deletion require owner.
Admin revocation and membership changes share pod locking.
Missing sign-in -> 401; missing local profile -> 403.
Insufficient role -> 403; foreign private pod -> 404.
end note
  Auth --> API: Authorized mutation or error
end
API --> Client: Route response after request transaction completes
note over API: Health and framework documentation bypass authentication.
@enduml
